{"name":"High Drama","hex":"#9a3843","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"high drama","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An event or atmosphere of strong emotion, typically of anxiety or excitement."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/high_drama"}],"entries":[{"title":"High Drama","blocks":[{"text":"High Drama is the fifth studio album and first covers album by American singer Adam Lambert. It was released on February 24, 2023, through More Is More and BMG."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/23/High_Drama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_Drama","wikidata":"Q120176613"},{"title":"Drama","blocks":[{"text":"Drama is the specific mode of fiction represented in performance: a play, opera, mime, ballet, etc., performed in a theatre, or on radio or television. Considered as a genre of poetry in general, the dramatic mode has been contrasted with the epic and the lyrical modes ever since Aristotle's Poetics —the earliest work of dramatic theory."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/The_Battle_of_Bosworth_Field_-_A_Scene_from_the_Great_Drama_of_History.jpg/330px-The_Battle_of_Bosworth_Field_-_A_Scene_from_the_Great_Drama_of_History.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drama","wikidata":"Q25372"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Books_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.png/500px-Books_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Books_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.png/500px-Books_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%